('CIT_REN_ACHAIAH_EXOD','ENT_REN_ACHAIAH','SRC_HEBREW_BIBLE','The Bible (KJV), Exodus 14:19-21 (basis of the 72-fold Name)','Exodus 14:19-21','And the angel of God, which went before the camp of Israel, removed and went behind them; and the pillar of the cloud went from before their face, and stood behind them: And it came between the camp of the Egyptians and the camp of Israel; and it was a cloud and darkness to them, but it gave light by night to these: so that the one came not near the other all the night.','King James Version',1611,'https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/10','https://www.sefaria.org/Exodus.14.19','primary-verbatim','The 72-letter Name (Shem ha-Mephorash) and its 72 angels derive from Exodus 14:19-21 (three verses of 72 Hebrew letters each). The individual angel names and zodiacal attributions are a medieval/Renaissance kabbalistic systematisation (cf. Kircher, Oedipus Aegyptiacus; Lenain) — verify the specific angel.',true,'Scriptural basis of the Shem ha-Mephorash; the specific angel name/attributes are a Renaissance kabbalistic derivation — confirm.',DATE '2026-06-18','derived-source attachment: Exodus 14:19-21 verbatim (KJV) as the scriptural origin of the 72 angels',1),
